DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't try to catch the AI knife.</b> The Nasdaq fell 5.5% into a confirmed correction and the chip index about 12%; one oversold day does not equal a buy signal — wait for breadth to improve (highs vs lows) before adding risk.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Extreme fear (Fear & Greed 20) and a VIX near 28 are when dollar-cost averaging into broad funds works better than guessing the bottom.",
"<b>The election trade cut both ways.</b> Wednesday's relief rally fully reversed Thursday on AI-regulation fears; don't build a portfolio around one political headline.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> The selloff was concentrated in chips and data-center names; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on AI.",
"<b>Rates can still rise in December.</b> CME FedWatch still shows about 81.5% odds of a hike on 9 Dec even as the 10Y eased to ~4.84%; avoid new high-interest debt and keep some cash/short bonds.",
"<b>Fuel is volatile, not fixed.</b> Brent snapped back to ~$98 after crashing below $95; budget for another spike if tanker attacks or Iran talks fail.",
"<b>Gold is working as a hedge again.</b> Near $4,095 after the flight to safety; if you hold some, keep it a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is near $76k (−5.6%); don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: selective and patient.</b> The SET (1,497.99) is just under 1,500 with support cited at 1,480. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, PTTEP, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); energy yields rose as PTT/PTTEP prices fell — check payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 20 = Extreme Fear, flat vs Wednesday and down from about 31 a week ago. Momentum, put/call, VIX and safe-haven demand are in extreme fear after Thursday's AI selloff."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated: tanker attacks and Houthi claims lifted spillover risk even as Qatar mediation and the 10-11 Nov Abu Dhabi talks continue, and Eurasia cut both deal and strike odds."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 6.4 = extreme fear: Thursday's 4.4% drop pushed the index deep below its trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 41.8 = fear (147 NYSE highs vs 224 lows Thursday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 45.4 = neutral on CNN's component, but the session was a broad AI/tech wipeout."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 8.4 = extreme fear: protection demand surged with the selloff."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 2.1 = extreme fear: the VIX closed about 28.2 Thursday, up from about 16.6 Wednesday."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 0.6 = extreme fear: bonds and gold beat stocks as equities sold off."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 34.4 = fear: junk demand is weak but less extreme than early in the week."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 62: Qatar mediation continues and strike odds were cut slightly, but deal odds fell and Hormuz stays shut. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 43 (slightly down): Abu Dhabi talks are still set for 10-11 Nov while Ukraine struck Russian refineries."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 74 (up): tanker incidents, Houthi claims and Yanbu alerts lifted spillover even as oil only partly recovered."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 16: Qatar still mediates US-Iran and Abu Dhabi Ukraine talks are confirmed."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats in our sources."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,354 Thursday (−4.36%), the worst day since April 2025."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −3.44% Thursday to about 51,523."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −5.52% Thursday to about 24,315; confirmed a >10% correction from its 6 Oct high."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.84% Thursday, down about 5bp on a flight to safety."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$90.5 (+2.7%) Thursday after Wednesday's crash to about $88."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$98.3 (+3.8%) Thursday; Hormuz is still effectively shut."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.26/gal (AAA, 5 Nov), edging down and below the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,095 (+0.5%) Thursday as equities sold off; $4,000 is support."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$76k = bearish: it fell with the AI trade after holding above $80k Wednesday."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September. October CPI is due 10 Nov."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 81.5% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec as of 5 Nov."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. Last noted about 101.8 (2 Nov); the Bloomberg dollar gauge rose 0.3% Tuesday on strong jobs data."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.7 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,497.99 Thu 5 Nov (−0.27%), just under 1,500; brokers cite support 1,480 and resistance 1,500."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿39.3M on 5 Nov (tiny); local institutions +฿1.03B, brokers −฿1.06B (InfoQuest/SET)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
